# Prettier is non-idempotent on this file and corrupts it a little more each run.
#
# The lesson displays Angular template syntax inside a <pre>, which means escaping
# braces as `{{ '{{' }}`. One of those interpolations sits on a line past the print
# width, and Prettier's angular parser tries to wrap it — inserting a newline INSIDE
# the quoted string. That newline is content, so it renders as blank lines in the code
# sample, and the next run inserts another one.
#
# Every other brace-escaped lesson formats cleanly and is checked; this one is pinned
# to its hand-formatted version until the upstream wrapping bug is fixed.
